System 573: frame profile taps out of the PSX core (Tier-3 #1-#3).

Run B (2026-09-17) measured the 573 side and found nothing: with ddrextrm in
gameplay the flash wait, the digital-board wait and the CD fetch are each ~0% of
the second, and the watchdog -- the intended frame meter -- turned out to be a
fixed 30 Hz task in this title (30 kicks/s in the attract screens that run at full
speed just as much as in the slow gameplay). So the run produced no frame rate at
all, and the time the game is losing is being lost inside the PSX core.

These are five signals that already exist in psx_top, brought out unchanged:
  dbg573_flip       GP1(05) "start of display area" write = the game's buffer
                    flip, one per RENDERED frame. This is the missing number.
  dbg573_vblank     the GPU's VBLANK irq, ~60/s: the reference to read it against.
  dbg573_cpupaused  cpuPaused -- the CPU is stopped while a DMA owns the bus.
  dbg573_cpustall   stallNext -- the CPU is stalled on a memory request.
  dbg573_gpubusy /  not SS_Idle_gpu / not SS_Idle_mdec -- the drawing engine and
  dbg573_mdecbusy   the MDEC video decoder are working.
Nothing is driven INTO the core and no existing signal changes, so this cannot
alter behaviour; rtl/s573_prof_gpu.v counts them and the HPS prints them once a
second.

diff --git a/rtl/psx_top.vhd b/rtl/psx_top.vhd
--- a/rtl/psx_top.vhd	2026-09-17 21:00:01.408000955 +0000
+++ b/rtl/psx_top.vhd	2026-09-17 20:53:46.396200415 +0000
@@ -251,7 +251,17 @@
       Cheats_BusWriteData   : out    std_logic_vector(31 downto 0);
       Cheats_Bus_ena        : out    std_logic := '0';
       Cheats_BusReadData    : in     std_logic_vector(31 downto 0);
-      Cheats_BusDone        : in     std_logic
+      Cheats_BusDone        : in     std_logic;
+      -- System 573 frame profile (s573_prof.v). Observation only: five signals that
+      -- already exist here, brought out so the 573 side can count them per second.
+      -- dbg573_flip is the GP1(05) "start of display area" write, i.e. the game's
+      -- buffer flip = one rendered frame; the rest are occupancy levels.
+      dbg573_flip           : out    std_logic := '0';
+      dbg573_vblank         : out    std_logic := '0';
+      dbg573_cpupaused      : out    std_logic := '0';
+      dbg573_cpustall       : out    std_logic := '0';
+      dbg573_gpubusy        : out    std_logic := '0';
+      dbg573_mdecbusy       : out    std_logic := '0'
    );
 end entity;
 
@@ -754,6 +764,15 @@
       end if;
    end process;
  
+   -- ---- System 573 frame profile taps (observation only) ----
+   dbg573_flip      <= '1' when (bus_gpu_write = '1' and bus_gpu_addr = x"4" and
+                                 bus_gpu_dataWrite(29 downto 24) = "000101") else '0';
+   dbg573_vblank    <= irq_VBLANK;
+   dbg573_cpupaused <= cpuPaused;
+   dbg573_cpustall  <= stallNext;
+   dbg573_gpubusy   <= not SS_Idle_gpu;
+   dbg573_mdecbusy  <= not SS_Idle_mdec;
+
    SS_idle    <= SS_Idle_gpu and SS_Idle_mdec and SS_Idle_cd and SS_idle_spu and SS_idle_pad and SS_idle_irq and SS_idle_cpu and SS_idle_gte and SS_idle_dma;
    
    Pause_Idle <= SS_Idle_gpu and SS_Idle_mdec and Pause_idle_cd and SS_idle_spu and SS_idle_pad and SS_idle_irq and SS_idle_cpu and SS_idle_gte and SS_idle_dma; 
